BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 660.00 Tm (Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 637.77 Tm (Gatekeeper opens with the headline loss: both Google and Facebook paid over a hundred million dollars to fraudulent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 622.55 Tm (vendors, which the speaker pins on one simple truth, that those vendors were never properly onboarded [-L_45dSkyaE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 607.32 Tm (@ 00:00:00]. Charted's Marlin traces the cheaper, more frequent version of the same failure: informal Excel or CSV) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 592.10 Tm (vendor updates are prone to potential fraud, carry incorrect formatting and lack validation, and a vendor who fat-fingers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 576.87 Tm (one extra digit into an ACH account number triggers a returned payment and a delayed payment, while a wrong address) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 561.65 Tm (sends the check to the wrong place and the error ripples into three-way match, month-end reconciliation and accruals) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 546.42 Tm (until it delays the close [1wlmLTmDAfc @ 00:07:23]. PROKURIA names the blind spots underneath: fragmented) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 531.20 Tm (data, suppliers asked for the same thing over and over, spreadsheet-and-email workflows that are slow and error-prone,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 515.97 Tm (expired insurance nobody catches, and vendor data stuck in one place while the ERP sits somewhere else) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 500.75 Tm ([_R1e9FCXKyI @ 00:02:17]. Peakflo's counter is verification at entry, showing a green tick when tax and bank details) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 485.52 Tm (validate and a red tag when bank account verification fails so the vendor must re-enter, but it warns that its GSTIN,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 470.30 Tm (PAN and MSME validation is only available for entities in India [Y400sNeYMUw @ 00:02:17].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 455.07 Tm (AVC-Licensing's D365 consolidation is the most candid failure ledger any speaker offers. Across 30 legal entities,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 439.85 Tm (nearly 8,000 vendor records mapped to about 6,800 master accounts, and the trap was not duplicates but duplicates that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 424.62 Tm (disagreed: a survivor record on hold, a retired record holding a tax ID the survivor lacked, two records of one supplier) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 409.40 Tm (paying into different bank accounts, and legitimate differences such as default ledger accounts that had to stay local) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 394.17 Tm ([8S2AXmoUSJY @ 00:01:03]. The team ran five full rehearsals on a copy of production, cut over in about 4 hours) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 378.95 Tm (inside a planned weekend window with a point-in-time restore as fallback, and still found Fabric and Power BI reports) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 363.72 Tm (pointing at old vendor references, fixed at the source and resynced in about a day; they refuse to claim an ROI they) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 348.50 Tm (never measured [8S2AXmoUSJY @ 00:02:41]. LeadSquared's Ashish describes the no-system version of the mess:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 333.27 Tm (details on Excel or paper in the field, verbal commitments nobody records, documents nobody can find, security) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 318.05 Tm (concerns, falling productivity and, ultimately, onboarding the wrong set of vendors [mR8B4VcLNjU @ 00:14:28].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 302.82 Tm (When Shivani polled the webinar audience, 36% named onboarding time as their top challenge, the stage where the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 287.60 Tm (most time goes [mR8B4VcLNjU @ 00:19:28].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 272.37 Tm (The economics traps sit on both sides of the table. 10 Min For Supply Chain runs the working-capital math on $50,000) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 257.15 Tm (of monthly purchases: moving from upfront payment to net 60 is worth roughly $100,000 of supplier financing under a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 241.92 Tm (simplified steady-state assumption, but only if the full monthly purchases qualify and the payment cycle is established,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 226.70 Tm (with invoice timing, shipment schedules and credit limits moving the real number [vdxHe8A6Tkk @ 00:02:11]. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 211.47 Tm (same speaker flags the two ways that gain evaporates: a volume commitment that forces you to buy unnecessary) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 196.25 Tm (inventory, and a supplier who raises prices or removes discounts in exchange for longer terms, so the total cost has to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 181.02 Tm (be recalculated; jumping straight from upfront to net 60 with a supplier who has little experience with your business is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 165.80 Tm (the named mistake [vdxHe8A6Tkk @ 00:02:42]. Finconvo Animation's interview guide adds the credibility check) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 150.57 Tm (every buyer gets tested on: explain the original quotation, the action taken and the final result, and do not claim savings) Tj ET
